# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the C tests (Linux; macOS ASan does not check leaks).
#
# Monitor (scull-pty) frees its native lock from a Kotlin/Native Cleaner, which runs only after the
# garbage collector finds the monitor unreachable. A short test exits before that happens, so every
# lock a freed terminal held (its FairLock, the PTY's and the child's monitors) is still allocated at
# exit. Nothing else is suppressed.
leak:scull_monitor_new
